luajit_generators/avro_packets/README.md:A LuaJIT-based DSL for generating C header files from Avro-like schema definitions. Designed for embedded systems with minimal runtime overhead.
luajit_generators/avro_packets/README.md:1. **Build-time generation** — LuaJIT reads schema definitions and emits static C headers. No runtime parsing or schema interpretation on the target.
luajit_generators/avro_packets/README.md:2. **Zero-copy encoding** — Structs are memory-mapped directly to wire format. Encode/decode are simple `memcpy` operations.
luajit_generators/avro_packets/README.md:3. **Per-record packet sizing** — Each record type gets its own packet structure sized exactly to its payload. No wasted space from max-sized buffers.
luajit_generators/avro_packets/README.md:4. **User-controlled allocation** — Generated code operates on caller-provided pointers. User decides stack, static, heap, or arena allocation.
luajit_generators/avro_packets/README.md:6. **Position-based indexing** — Record index is determined by declaration order in the schema. Dense tables, no sparse 256-entry arrays.
luajit_generators/avro_packets/README.md:- `index` — Record type (0-based position in schema)
luajit_generators/avro_packets/README.md:- `len` — Payload size in bytes
luajit_generators/avro_packets/README.md:- `payload` — Struct data (little-endian, packed)
